  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan 17.10.2025; EXISTING DRAWINGS 25_1002_101 RevC 09.10.2025; EXISTING SECTION PROPOSED SECTION 25_1002_103 RevD 08.12.2025; PROPOSED DRAWINGS 25_1002_102 RevD 08.12.2025; Flood Risk Assessment ref: U0755 FRA-v1 Dec 2025; Energy Statement; HIGHWAY SAFETY IMPACT FORM.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding condition 2, prior to first occupation of the development hereby permitted, Cycle parking, shall be provided within the site in accordance with the following requirements:\r\ro Provision of a minimum of FOUR long stay cycle parking spaces in the front garden (two per flat).\r\ro in an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m;\r\ro secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\ro fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities.\r",
    "The refuse and recycling storage hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details and thereafter maintained unless otherwise in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The residential units hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the Building Regulations Optional requirement G2 for water consumption of no more than 105 litres or less per head per day (excluding allowance of up to five litres for external water consumption) has been complied with. The measures shall thereafter be permanently retained.\r\rReason: To promote water conservation and efficiency measures in all new developments and where possible in the retrofitting of existing stock in accordance with Policy SI 5 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy CP21 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010).\r"
  ],
